bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 28th March 2025</strong></span></span></p>\r\n<p>\r\n	<span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span style=\"font-family:bookman old style,serif;\"><strong>,</strong></span></span></p>\r\n<p>\r\n	<span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span style=\"font-family:bookman old style,serif;\"><strong>Principal</strong> <strong>Investigator</strong> <strong>ECCT/25/02/06,</strong></span></span></p>\r\n<p>\r\n	<span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span style=\"font-family:bookman old style,serif;\"><strong>Sit cupiditate similique iure aut,</strong></span></span></p>\r\n<p>\r\n	<span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span style=\"font-family:bookman old style,serif;\">Dear Sir/Madam,</span></span></p>\r\n<p>\r\n	<span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span style=\"font-family:bookman old style,serif;\"><strong><u>Re: ECCT/25/02/06 : Initial Approval; <p>\r\n	Test Input</p>\r\n&nbsp; Voluptatem Doloremque in amet</u></strong></span><strong style=\"font-family: &quot;bookman old style&quot;, serif;\"><u>.</u></strong></span></p>\r\n<p>\r\n	<span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span style=\"font-family:bookman old style,serif;\">Reference is made to the above study.</span></span></p>\r\n<p>\r\n	<span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span style=\"font-family:bookman old style,serif;\">We acknowledge receipt of the following documents;</span></span></p>\r\n<div style=\"margin-left: 15px;\">\r\n	<span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><span style=\"font-family:bookman old style,serif;\">1. Cover Letter (Should list all the submitted documents, their version numbers and dates)<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1737\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_18_07_49_27.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025  Version 1<br>2. The Study Protocol<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1738\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>3. Registration of the study at Pan African Clinical Trials Registry https://pactr.samrc.ac.za<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1744\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_17_11_53_20_6.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>4. Patient Information leaflet and Informed consent form<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1745\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_4.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>5. Investigators Brochure/Package inserts<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1746\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_17_12_10_38_23.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>6. Investigational Medicinal Product Dossier (IMPD)<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1747\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_5.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>7. Adequate data and information from previous studies and Phases to support carrying out of the current study<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1748\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_6.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>8. Stability data of the investigational product<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1749\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_17_12_10_38_24.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>9. GMP certificate of the investigational product from the site of manufacture<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1750\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_17_12_10_38_25.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>10. Certificate of Analysis of the investigational product<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1751\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_7.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025  Version 2<br>11. Pictorial Sample of the investigational products. This sample should include the text of the labeling to be used<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1752\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_8.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>12. Signed investigator(s) CV(s) including that of study Pharmacist (NB: The CV should include the current workload of the Principal Investigator )<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1764\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_13.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>13. Evidence of contractual agreement between sponsor and Principal Investigator.<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1763\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_17_12_10_38_32.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>14. Evidence of recent GCP training of the core study staff<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1762\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_12.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>15. DSMB Charter including the composition and meeting schedule<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1761\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_17_12_10_38_31.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>16. Detailed budget of the study<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1760\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_11.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>17. Financial declaration by Sponsor and/or PI http://45.79.161.190:8080/admin/attachments/download/1736<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1759\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_17_12_10_38_30.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>18. Signed Declaration by Sponsor or Principal investigator that the study will be carried out according to the protocol and applicable laws, regulations and GCP requirements. http://45.79.161.190:8080/admin/attachments/download/1732<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1758\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_17_12_10_38_29.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>19. Indemnity cover for PI,  investigators and study Pharmacist. <br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1757\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_17_12_10_38_28.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>20. Clinical Trials Insurance cover for study participants<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1756\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_17_12_10_38_27.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>21. Copy of favorable opinion letter from the local Ethics Review Committee (ERC).<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1755\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_10.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>22. Copy of current Practice Licenses for the Investigators and study Pharmacist<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1754\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_17_12_10_38_26.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>23. Copy of approval letter(s) from collaborating institutions or other regulatory authorities, if applicable<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1753\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_9.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>24. For multicentre/multi-site studies, a site specific addendum for each of the proposed sites including among other things the sitesâ€™ capacity to carry out the study i.e personnel, equipment, laboratory etc<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1743\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_3.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>25. A signed statement by the applicant indicating that all information contained in, or referenced by, the application is complete and accurate and is not false or misleading.<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1742\">art_monthly_report_2025_02_18_07_55_57_2.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>26. Payment of fees<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1741\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_17_12_10_38_22.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br>27. Statistical Analysis Plan<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1740\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_18_07_49_27_3.xls</a> <br>28. Signed Checklist<br><a href=\"http://45.79.161.190:8080/attachments/download/1739\">line_list_of_all_client_2025_02_18_07_49_27_2.xls</a> dated: 19th February 2025 <br></span></span></div>\r\n<p>\r\n	<span style=\"font-size:12px;\">After review of the documents, the Pharmacy and Poisons Board Expert Committee on Clinical Trials notes the following:</span></p>\r\n<p>\r\n	<span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>Trial category workspace</strong><br>Amet illum labore <br><br><strong>Trial category comments</strong><br>Ab nisi omnis qui ea<br><br><strong>Trial phase workspace</strong><br>Consequatur repudian<br><br><strong>Trial phase comments (if in disagreement with the study phase proposed): </strong><br>Est in sed veritatis<br><br><strong>Therapeutic condition workspace</strong><br>Aut aperiam suscipit<br><br><strong>Brief description of the disease</strong><br>Reprehenderit delect<br><br><strong>Brief discussion of clinical pharmacokinetic data, efficacy and safety data described in the IB from previous trials /previously investigated indications(s) for the IMP(s). Non-clinical studies may also be discussed for early or FIH clinical trials. Consideration should be given to the justification provided based on the non-clinical data, for the proposed starting dose, dose steps, and maximum exposure</strong><br>Est temporibus corr<br><br><strong>Assessorâ€™s discussion on the clinical development:</strong><br>Molestiae minus sit<br><br><strong>Consider what is new in this trial, the clinical relevance, and the medical need that the trial aims to address</strong><br>Dignissimos amet ex<br><br><strong>Clinical Trial Rationale comments</strong><br>Quae voluptatum debi<br><br><strong>Consider if there are established primary endpoints for this type of study/indication, do they match the goals, are they validated?</strong><br>Fuga Alias ut volup<br><br><strong>Primary objectives comments</strong><br>Possimus explicabo<br><br><strong>Secondary objectives workspace</strong><br>Magni molestias omni<br>